hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15494","Waki and Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, both said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Sufyan ibn Abd Allah al-Thaqafi, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, say to me in Islam a statement I will not ask about it anyone other than you. Abu Muawiyah said: after you. He said: Say: I believe in Allah, then be upright."
"15495","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Yala ibn Ata, from Abd Allah ibn Sufyan, from his father, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, inform me of a matter in Islam I will not ask about it anyone after you. He said: Say: I believe in Allah, then be upright. He said: O Messenger of Allah, then what should I guard? He said: So he pointed with his hand to his tongue."
"15496","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Ibrahim, meaning Ibn Sad, narrated to us, Ibn Shihab narrated to us, and Yazid ibn Harun, he said: Ibrahim informed us, he said: Ibn Shihab narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Maiz al-Amiri, from Sufyan ibn Abd Allah al-Thaqafi, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, narrate to me a matter I hold fast to. He said: Say: My Lord is Allah, then be upright. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the greatest you fear for me? He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took his own tongue, then said: This. Yazid said in his hadith: With the tip of his own tongue."
"15497","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, informed us, he said: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Maiz, from Sufyan ibn Abd Allah al-Thaqafi, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, narrate to me a matter I hold fast to. He said: Say: My Lord is Allah, then be upright. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the most fearful you fear for me? He said: So he took his own tongue, then said: This."
